/**
 * Backlog clean-up (phase 5, started 2026-11-23): apply the proven sender rules to the old inbox.
 *
 * It only adds labels, archives (removes from the Inbox) and marks read. It never deletes, trashes, sends,
 * or creates labels. It skips mail from the last 2 days (the daily sort's job) and anything to or from a
 * school address (the school module's job).
 *
 * Functions (pick one in the menu at the top and click Run):
 *   dryRun        Changes nothing. Counts what each rule would do and writes a report to the
 *                 "Backlog sort" spreadsheet in Drive (tab "Dry run").
 *   runLive       Applies the rules. Every thread it changes is written to the "Undo log" tab.
 *   archiveOldTriaged   Archives and marks read the old threads that already have a *Triage/FYI or
 *                 *Triage/Bulk label but were never archived. Logged too. Run only if Dom agrees.
 *   tallySenders  Read-only. Lists who sent the old inbox threads no rule matched ("Unruled senders" tab).
 *   sweepDryRun   Changes nothing. Counts what sweepLive would do ("Sweep dry run" tab). Run after runLive.
 *   sweepLive     After the rules (Dom, 2026-11-24): files school threads over 1 month old under their School
 *                 label as FYI and archives them, then archives (as FYI, no folder) threads no rule matches
 *                 whose newest message is over 1 year old. Logged in the "Undo log" tab like runLive.
 *   undo          Reads the "Undo log" tab and reverses it: removes the labels it added and puts archived
 *                 threads back in the Inbox. It can't mark them unread again.
 *   resetProgress Forgets where a run got to, so the next run starts from the first rule.
 *
 * Apps Script stops a run after 6 minutes, so each function stops itself at about 4 and remembers where it
 * got to. If the log says "Not finished", click Run again until it says "Done".
 *
 * Needs the Gmail API service switched on (left sidebar: Services > + > Gmail API > Add). runLive and
 * archiveOldTriaged use it to change up to 1,000 messages per call.
 *
 * RULES is generated from config/sender-rules.yaml by build_rules.py. Don't edit it by hand.
 */

